<header><p class="st-kicker">chiefdom · France and the Low Countries</p><h1 class="st-title">Helvii</h1><p class="st-meta">300 BCE – 121 BCE (approx.) · capital Alba Helviorum</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Gallic people of the Vivarais who stayed loyal to Rome in 52 BCE and from whose land Caesar crossed the snowbound Cévennes.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The Helvii lived on the right bank of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhone">Rhône</a> in the modern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardeche">Ardèche</a>, at the edge of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/massif-central">Massif Central</a>. Their land became part of the Roman Province after 121 BCE.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Caesar names <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-valerius-caburus">Gaius Valerius Caburus</a>, who had received Roman citizenship from the governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-valerius-flaccus">Gaius Valerius Flaccus</a>, an early example of a Gallic noble family adopting Roman ways. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-valerius-donnotaurus">Gaius Valerius Donnotaurus</a> was the leading man of the people in 52 BCE.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 52 BCE the Helvii were attacked by the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/gabali">Gabali</a> and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/arverni">Arverni</a> for their loyalty, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-valerius-donnotaurus">Donnotaurus</a> was killed in the fighting. Caesar marched through their territory and crossed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cevennes">Cévennes</a> in deep snow to strike the Arverni. Their Roman town was <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alba-helviorum">Alba Helviorum</a> (Alba-la-Romaine), and the region later became the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vivarais">Vivarais</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="chiefdom, 300 BCE – 121 BCE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><ellipse cx="44" cy="56" rx="16" ry="24"/><path d="M44 34 V78"/><path d="M68 20 V84"/><path d="M68 20 L63 30 H73 Z"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">chiefdom</p><p class="st-emblem-region">France and the Low Countries</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:53.73%;width:3.56%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>300 BCE – 121 BCE (approx.)</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>chiefdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Alba Helviorum</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Gaius Valerius Donnotaurus</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Celtic polytheism</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gaulish</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>France</dd></dl></aside></div>

